<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaston IV of Béarn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1131</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Gaston IV the Crusader</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaston IV, Viscount of Béarn, known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader</a>, took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a> and was among the leaders at the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 1099. He later fought alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon">Alfonso I of Aragon</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a>, helping take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> in 1118, and was killed fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> in 1131.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaston-iv-of-bearn.jpg" alt="Gaston IV of Béarn" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexandre Lacauchie · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gaston_dans_J%C3%A9rusalem.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
